A||||5||Leadfoot||Cracked tranny?!||||9||
Z||000000||Leadfoot||06-18-2001||07:58 PM||||I was putting my rebuild engine on the cradle the other day when I noticed near the rear transmission mount bracket (left side of the transmission) that there was a crack.  The 1/2 crack is right smack dab in the middle of the 2 bracket mounting holes.  Now I am not sure if it is just a surface crack but it sure can explain why I always am leaking oil even after I replaced the axle shaft seals.  I was wondering if anyone here had noticed something similar on their 4 speed trans?  By the way, this is off an 85 2m6 se.  God I hope it's nothing serious.  I was so looking forward into finally driving my baby this weekend.  Crud in the mud!!  Do you guys think this is serious?||||reg||9
Z||000001||cadaver||06-18-2001||09:41 PM||||If you dont think it will crack farther then seal it. Hell even if you do think it will crack farther I would seal it and drive it till it failed||||reg||1
Z||000002||starfighter007@msn.com||06-18-2001||10:21 PM||||yes I would have to agree on sealing this crack and if it is stress crack maybe go to a welding shop that welds aluminum and see what they could for you good luck||||reg||10
Z||000003||Formula88||06-19-2001||01:00 PM||||I'd either have a shop weld it, or use some JB Weld on it to seal it.  I've seen blocks cracked into the water jacket sealed with that stuff run for years.  ||||reg||4
Z||000004||theogre||06-19-2001||07:36 PM||||case crack causes... <P>basic stress cracks... rare but it happens.<BR>broken/shot rubber mount... real common.<BR>over torqued or wrong bolt... happens allot.<P>Epoxy is an option but you have to get everything clean as posible. Brake parts cleaner would work well here.<P>Alumnum is porous. after you clean it get it good and warm with a PROPANE torch to drive oil out of the metal. Then clean it again. This should get rid of allot of the oil so the adhesive bites.<P>Welding on something like that is tricky. You can't just shove the parts together. Need to grind out a bit of a wedge along the crack so you get a good deep weld. This is often a real pain with a crack. Better it if just broke off.<P>If you do get a decent repair start looking for another tranny anyway. The odds are good it could crack again.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Leadfoot||06-19-2001||07:55 PM||||Thanks for the input guys.  Man, is it a bummer when you think you fixed everything, only to find you missed a spot.  I just replaced the mounts and put a generous amount of JB Weld on the crack.  Hope it lasts.  I just don't feel like dropping the cradle again.  I had a heck of a time taking it off (by myself, in a 1/2 car garage, uphill, no air conditioning, with wooden wrenches.....o.k. so I am stretching the truth a little)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> since every darn bolt was rust tight.  Well next time shouldn't be so bad since I used s.s. all around.  Although it would be nice to get a 5 speed Getrag. I just got to find one at a reasonable price.  That shouldn't be so hard since it looks like I am the only one looking for one.........NOT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">    ||||reg||1
